{
  "about": "Graphs folded, merged and routed as a graph's View menu and style graph say (editor spec §25: untangle_hubs, untangle_groups, untangle_merge, untangle_routing, view_switch_defaults), drawn the same by the plugin's core and by graph_svg.py. Each case is a note's gql blocks, each block a list of lines; the view it is drawn in, if any (its name only: the whole graph is drawn, styled and switched as that view is); the switches turned from where they start (hubs, groups and merge, each true or false; a switch not given starts as the plugin's settings hold it by default, as the style graph merges links, or as the view was saved as shown); and the busy hubs and groups opened again. For every case both give the same problems reading each style and, for every graph drawn, the same Graphviz source in each direction laid out, byte for byte. The expected answers are the core's, run live: packages/core/test/layout-parity.test.js holds graph_svg.py to the core on these cases, and tests/test_graph_svg_folds.py does the same from the Python side.",
